  id: Levator_nasolabialis_muscle.L
  partName: Levator Nasolabialis Muscle L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'This muscle lifts the upper lip and dilates the nostrils, playing a key role
    in both facial expression and respiratory function. It is especially active during
    sniffing, allowing increased airflow into the nasal passages. '
  - In addition to its respiratory role, it contributes to expressions such as curiosity,
    alertness, or mild aggression. It works in coordination with surrounding muscles
    to control movements of the nose and upper lip, enhancing both sensory intake
    and expressive communication.
